{
  "_comment": [
    "Key skeleton of a stored drag-and-drop editor document, page-rooted form. Values are",
    "placeholders; what matters here are the key names, the nesting and which levels carry style.",
    "The second valid shape is this document without the 'page' wrapper -- the editor's save",
    "callback returns the page itself, and it is stored unchanged. Normalize before reading:",
    "page = document['page'] if that key holds an object, else the document.",
    "An email created without a body stores nothing at all; read that as",
    "{\"page\":{\"body\":{\"webFonts\":[]},\"rows\":[]}}.",
    "'kt-decisions' and 'kt-ai-blocks' are KlickTipp's own keys, not the editor's: they are",
    "stripped before rendering, so an HTML round trip deletes them."
  ],
